From: Keir Fraser <keirf@google.com>
Date: Thu Apr 23 14:12:51 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: kvm: arm64: Fix buddy race in __hyp_put_page()

__hyp_put_page() decrements the page refcount to zero before taking
the pool lock and initialising the allocator's list_head. This races with
the buddy page also being freed, and looking for its free buddy.

Fix this by proactively taking the pool lock if we will decrement the
refcount to zero. This requires us to replace a fetch-and-add with
a cmpxchg loop.

Bug: 495629978
Change-Id: Ie307ec27de86777109c6e2d53835b128a729e460
Signed-off-by: Keir Fraser <keirf@google.com>

[gki6677 reshape note - 2026-11-02, Z.ai]
Reshaped for the 6.6.77 pin: upstream's post-state accounts free_pages
via update_free_pages() (which also tracks pool->min_free_pages);
that helper and the min_free_pages field are introduced by an
intermediate allocator commit between the shipped earliest twin of
"Fix hyp_pool::free_pages" (our 0035) and this fix, and the field
does not exist at the pin (struct hyp_pool untouched - KMI-safe).
The race fix itself (cmpxchg_relaxed refcount loop + acquiring the
pool lock before the refcount reaches zero) is shipped verbatim;
the free_pages accounting keeps the pin's existing
WRITE_ONCE(pool->free_pages, ...) form with 0035's (1ULL << order)
correction. Verified: strict git apply on the pin replica.

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common d40232a360ca352e53a3f97fcd0efd6efbecee8b
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class B, RESHAPED for the pin; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/page_alloc.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/page_alloc.c
index a4b3790cb..9ac34fb6b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/page_alloc.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/page_alloc.c
@@ -158,9 +158,28 @@ static struct hyp_page *__hyp_extract_page(struct hyp_pool *pool,
 static void __hyp_put_page(struct hyp_pool *pool, struct hyp_page *p)
 {
 	u64 free_pages;
+	u16 seen_refcount, old_refcount;
+
+	for (old_refcount = READ_ONCE(p->refcount); ; old_refcount = seen_refcount) {
+		WARN_ON(old_refcount == 0);
+		if (old_refcount == 1) {
+			/*
+			 * Acquire the pool lock before we drop the refcount to
+			 * zero, thus avoiding a race with __find_buddy_avail()
+			 * finding us before we initialise our in-page
+			 * list_head.
+			 */
+			hyp_spin_lock(&pool->lock);
+		}
+		seen_refcount = cmpxchg_relaxed(
+			&p->refcount, old_refcount, old_refcount-1);
+		if (seen_refcount == old_refcount)
+			break;
+		if (old_refcount == 1)
+			hyp_spin_unlock(&pool->lock);
+	}
 
-	if (hyp_page_ref_dec_and_test(p)) {
-		hyp_spin_lock(&pool->lock);
+	if (old_refcount == 1) {
 		free_pages = pool->free_pages + (1ULL << p->order);
 		__hyp_attach_page(pool, p);
 		WRITE_ONCE(pool->free_pages, free_pages);
